---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="HostFleet moved on from generic web hosting" description="HostFleet retired its old generic web-hosting library and now focuses on AI hosting and deployment infrastructure.">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pt-16 pb-24 prose">
    <div class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-accent)]">site pivot</div>
    <h1>HostFleet retired its old web-hosting library</h1>
    <p>HostFleet no longer operates as a generic web-hosting review site. We now focus on AI hosting, deployment infrastructure, edge runtimes, GPU hosts, and the real-world platforms where AI apps actually run.</p>
    <p>If you landed here from an older HostFleet article, that page has been retired from the active site because it no longer fits the product direction.</p>
    <h2>What HostFleet covers now</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/ai-hosting/">AI hosting and inference platforms</a></li>
      <li><a href="/deploy-ai-apps/">Deployment paths for AI-generated and AI-powered apps</a></li>
      <li><a href="/edge/">Edge runtimes and modern web infrastructure</a></li>
      <li><a href="/about/">Methodology and editorial policy</a></li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Why the old pages were retired</h2>
    <p>Leaving them live kept sending mixed signals about what HostFleet is for. The site now has a tighter mission, and the public surface needs to match it.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
